      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining Embedding Provider**\n\nOkay, I'm setting up `embed_batch.py`. I've decided to go with Google Cloud's `vertexai.preview.language_models` for text embeddings. This should be a robust and scalable option for the batch processing. Now I need to figure out how to best integrate it into the file.\n\n\n**Implementing Embedding Batch**\n\nI'm making progress on `embed_batch.py`, focusing on the batch embedding function. I'm leveraging the `vertexai.preview.language_models.TextEmbeddingModel` to generate embeddings for a list of texts. I'll define a function to handle input lists and return the embeddings, managing imports and model instantiation within the Python file.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789865598099,
          "start": 1789865596824
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc4d9798001NRsc6w44j7AHz4",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc4d92bb001ddc0gRbCNibHic",
      "session_id": "ses_f43b26d54ffeXFKWPGVfmTCPsF",
